---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import { Badge, Card, Grid } from "webcoreui/astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import DeckSection from "@components/DeckSection.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="History - Replenish Guide"
    prev={{ name: "Introduction", href: "/" }}
    next={{ name: "Maindeck", href: "/analysis" }}
>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 3rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        History of the Deck
    </h1>

    <p
        style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-20); margin-bottom: 2rem;"
    >
        The story of Replenish spans over two decades. From its dominance in
        Type 2 (Standard) at the turn of the millennium, to its rebirth in
        Premodern fueled by rules changes, and finally its resilience in the
        face of bans. Here is a look at the archetypes' defining milestones.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h2>1. The Standard Origins (2000)</h2>
        <p>
            Replenish first made waves at the highest levels of competitive
            Magic during the 2000 World Championship. Hall of Famer Tom van de
            Logt piloted this list to a Top 8 finish. This Type 2 list leaned on
            fast mana like <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Sky Diamond">Sky Diamond</a
            > and <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Rishadan Port"
                >Rishadan Port</a
            > to slow opponents down, while using <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Mystical Tutor">Mystical Tutor</a
            > and <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Enlightened Tutor">Enlightened Tutor</a
            > for immense consistency. A single <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Energy Field">Energy Field</a
            > could buy infinite time until the combo was ready.
        </p>
        <p
            style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-40); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
        >
            <em
                >Source: <a
                    href="https://mtgtop8.com/event?e=9200&d=252726&f=ST"
                    target="_blank"
                    style="color: var(--w-color-info);"
                    >2000 World Championship Coverage (MTGTop8)</a
                ></em
            >
        </p>

        <Card>
            <div
                style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div>
                    <h3
                        style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                    >
                        2000 World Championship (Standard)
                    </h3>
                    <p
                        style="margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                    >
                        Played by Tom van de Logt
                    </p>
                </div>
                <Badge theme="info">Standard</Badge>
            </div>

            <Grid column={3} gap="lg">
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Enchantments"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Attunement" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Opalescence" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Parallax Wave" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Parallax Tide" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Energy Field" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Seal of Cleansing" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Seal of Removal" },
                        ]}
                    />
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Sorceries"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Replenish" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Wrath of God" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Instants"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Frantic Search" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Counterspell" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Enlightened Tutor" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Mystical Tutor" },
                        ]}
                    />
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Artifacts"
                        items={[{ count: 1, name: "Sky Diamond" }]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Lands"
                        items={[
                            { count: 9, name: "Island" },
                            { count: 8, name: "Plains" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Adarkar Wastes" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Rishadan Port" },
                        ]}
                    />
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Sideboard"
                        items={[
                            { count: 3, name: "Erase" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Daze" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Lilting Refrain" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Submerge" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Wrath of God" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Chill" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Circle of Protection: Black" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Cursed Totem" },
                            { count: 1, name: "Seal of Cleansing" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
            </Grid>
        </Card>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h2>2. The Errata Reversal (The Spark)</h2>
        <p>
            For many years in Premodern, Replenish was merely a fringe strategy.
            The card that changed everything was a rules update. Originally,
            Parallax cards received errata to prevent their "leave play"
            triggers from resolving before their "remove a counter" triggers
            (preventing permanent exile). When Wizards of the Coast reversed
            this errata to match the printed wording on the cards, the <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
            > + <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Opalescence"
                >Opalescence</a
            > permanent-exile loop was restored. This single change resurrected the
            archetype and propelled it to Tier 1 status.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h2>3. The Parallax Tide Era (Pre-Ban 2025)</h2>
        <p>
            With the errata reversed, players quickly realized that <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Parallax Tide">Parallax Tide</a
            > could permanently exile an opponent's lands just as easily as Wave exiled
            creatures. By late 2025, Parallax Tide Replenish variants accounted for
            nearly 30% of Top 8 finishes in major tournaments. It was a one-sided
            Armageddon that left opponents completely helpless.
        </p>
        <p
            style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-40); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
        >
            <em
                >Source: <a
                    href="https://squeeshouseofpizza.com/en-brl/pages/replenish-primer-brian-siu"
                    target="_blank"
                    style="color: var(--w-color-info);"
                    >Replenish Primer by Brian Siu</a
                ></em
            >
        </p>

        <Card>
            <div
                style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"
            >
                <div>
                    <h3
                        style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--w-color-primary-10);"
                    >
                        The Parallax Tide Era (Pre-Ban)
                    </h3>
                    <p
                        style="margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0; color: var(--w-color-primary-40);"
                    >
                        Typical 2025 Premodern Decklist
                    </p>
                </div>
                <Badge theme="warning">Premodern</Badge>
            </div>

            <Grid column={3} gap="lg">
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Enchantments"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Attunement" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Opalescence" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Parallax Wave" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Parallax Tide" },
                        ]}
                    />
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Sorceries"
                        items={[{ count: 4, name: "Replenish" }]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Instants"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Swords to Plowshares" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Frantic Search" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Intuition" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Mana Leak" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
                <div>
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Lands"
                        items={[
                            { count: 6, name: "Island" },
                            { count: 5, name: "Plains" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Flooded Strand" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Adarkar Wastes" },
                            { count: 4, name: "Ancient Tomb" },
                            { count: 2, name: "City of Traitors" },
                        ]}
                    />
                    <DeckSection
                        title="Sideboard"
                        items={[
                            { count: 4, name: "Meddling Mage" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Exalted Angel" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Seal of Cleansing" },
                            { count: 3, name: "Defense Grid" },
                            { count: 2, name: "Hydroblast" },
                        ]}
                    />
                </div>
            </Grid>
        </Card>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <h2>4. The Post-Ban Resurgence (2026 - Present)</h2>
        <p>
            On January 18, 2026, format curator Martin Berlin banned Parallax
            Tide, citing its oppressive, repetitive play patterns and
            insurmountable win rates. The community wrote the deck off, assuming
            it was dead without its primary lock piece.
        </p>
        <p>
            However, dedicated pilots proved them wrong. By replacing Tide with <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Decree of Silence">Decree of Silence</a
            > and relying more heavily on cards like <a
                href="#"
                class="card-hover"
                data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
            > and <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Exalted Angel"
                >Exalted Angel</a
            > out of the sideboard, the deck evolved from a pure combo lock into a
            resilient combo-control hybrid. You can check out the current, post-ban
            decklists on the <a
                href="/deck"
                style="color: var(--w-color-info); text-decoration: underline;"
                >Lists page</a
            >.
        </p>
    </div>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
